---
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import { href } from '../../site.config.mjs';
---
<section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="surfaces">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-eyebrow">FROM YOUR TERMINAL TO YOUR PIPELINE</p><h2 id="surfaces">Three surfaces, one runtime.</h2><p class="section-intro">Work interactively. Run unattended. Share a local server.</p></div><a class="section-link" href={href('docs/headless/')}>Meet the runtime <Icon name="right-arrow" size="18" /></a></div>
  <div class="surfaces-grid">
    <article class="surface-card"><h3>qq</h3><div class="surface-label">The interactive terminal</div><p>Opens in the current directory. Approvals appear in the transcript where the call is; many sessions, one screen.</p><pre><span class="prompt">$ </span>cd my-project &amp;&amp; qq</pre><a class="card-bottom" href={href('docs/tui/')}><span>Explore the TUI</span><Icon name="right-arrow" size="17" /></a></article>
    <article class="surface-card"><h3>qq run</h3><div class="surface-label">The headless runner</div><p>The same agent in a script or CI job. Read-only unless you say otherwise; JSONL out, meaningful exit codes.</p><pre><span class="prompt">$ </span>qq run <span class="flag">--approval</span> auto <span class="flag">--format</span> jsonl<br />  <span class="string">"Add a --dry-run flag and a test"</span></pre><a class="card-bottom" href={href('docs/headless/#exit-codes')}><span class="font-mono">Exit codes: 0 1 2 3 4 5 130</span><Icon name="right-arrow" size="17" /></a></article>
    <article class="surface-card"><h3>qq serve</h3><div class="surface-label">The shared local server</div><p>Several clients, one runtime, over HTTP and SSE. Random loopback port by default.</p><pre><span class="prompt">$ </span>qq serve <span class="flag">--bind</span> 127.0.0.1:4711</pre><a class="card-bottom" href={href('docs/headless/#qq-serve--a-persistent-server')}><span>Run a server</span><Icon name="right-arrow" size="17" /></a></article>
  </div>
  <p class="surface-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span>Same tools. Same policy. Same SQLite store. Everywhere.</p>
</section>
